---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';

const workerSnippet = `# Each krabka-connect-worker process runs one connector. Every flag also has a
# KRABKA_* environment variable; the connection URL is a secret, so pass it there.
export KRABKA_POSTGRES_URL='postgres://cdc_user:change-me@db.internal:5432/inventory'

krabka-connect-worker \\
  --connector-id postgres-inventory-cdc \\
  --kafka-bootstrap kafka:9092 \\
  --schema-registry-url http://schema-registry:8081 \\
  --postgres-slot krabka_inventory_slot \\
  --postgres-publication inventory_publication \\
  --postgres-schema public \\
  --postgres-tables orders,line_items,customers \\
  --topic-prefix db`;

const connectorCrSnippet = `apiVersion: krabka.io/v1alpha1
kind: KafkaConnector
metadata:
  name: postgres-inventory-cdc
  labels:
    krabka.io/cluster: demo
spec:
  type: postgresSource
  databaseUrl:
    name: inventory-db
    key: url
  schemaRegistryUrl: http://schema-registry:8081
  slot: krabka_inventory_slot
  publication: inventory_publication
  schema: public
  tables: [orders, line_items, customers]
  topicPrefix: db`;

const acceptanceTestSnippet = `# The Postgres CDC acceptance suite needs Docker. It starts Postgres and a schema
# registry in containers, runs the worker, force-kills it, restarts it, and checks
# that the records still arrive after the restart, including across an ALTER TABLE.
cargo test -p krabka-connect-worker --test postgres_cdc -- --ignored`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="PostgreSQL CDC Source Connector (pgoutput)"
  description="PostgreSQL change data capture (CDC) source connector over logical decoding (pgoutput) with checkpoint resumption in krabka-connect."
  currentSlug="/docs/connect-postgres"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 font-sans">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-1">
        Data Integration · Developer Preview
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">PostgreSQL CDC Source Connector</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Stream database change logs over logical decoding (<code class="text-krab-300 font-mono text-xs">pgoutput</code>) directly into Kafka topics via <code class="text-krab-300 font-mono text-xs">krabka-connect-postgres</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-xs text-amber-300 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-amber-200">Developer Preview Notice:</strong>
        The <code class="font-mono text-amber-200">krabka-connect</code> framework and its PostgreSQL CDC connector are currently in active development. Logical decoding and checkpoint resumption are exercised by a Docker-backed acceptance suite. The worker runs one connector per process.
      </div>

      <p>
        <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-connect-postgres</code> captures row-level inserts, updates, and deletes directly from PostgreSQL write-ahead logs using the native <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">pgoutput</code> logical replication stream. Each record carries the source LSN, transaction id, and commit timestamp, and DELETE events become tombstones. The connector registers its Protobuf key and value schemas with a Confluent-compatible Schema Registry at startup, and it needs no JVM sidecar. It does not take an initial snapshot: it emits only the changes that logical decoding makes available.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Connector Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        The connector framework is split across five modular crates in the <a href="https://github.com/krabka-io/krabka-connect" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-krab-400 hover:underline"><code>krabka-connect</code> repository</a>:
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase text-gray-400 font-sans">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Crate</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Role & Responsibility</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 font-sans">
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-krab-300">krabka-connect</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">The connector SPI: <code class="font-mono text-xs">Source</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs">Sink</code>, and <code class="font-mono text-xs">Converter</code> traits with checkpoint contracts.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-krab-300">krabka-connect-derive</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">Derive macros for declarative connector configuration schemas (<code class="font-mono text-xs">#[derive(ConnectorConfig)]</code>).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-krab-300">krabka-connect-postgres</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">PostgreSQL CDC source connector (<code class="font-mono text-xs">PostgresWalSource</code>) over <code class="font-mono text-xs">pgoutput</code> replication slots.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-krab-300">krabka-connect-worker</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">Connector worker runtime: polls sources, batches into Kafka producers, and checkpoints offsets.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-krab-300">krabka-replicator</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">Cluster-to-cluster replication engine wire-compatible with Kafka MirrorMaker 2.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Running the Worker</h2>
      <p>
        <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">krabka-connect-worker</code> is configured by flags or environment variables. It creates the replication slot, and the publication for the configured tables, when they are missing. Records go to <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">&lt;topic-prefix&gt;.&lt;schema&gt;.&lt;table&gt;</code>, for example <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">db.public.orders</code>. The library-level <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">PostgresSourceConfig</code> keys are <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">database_url</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">schema_registry_url</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">slot_name</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">publication_name</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">schema</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">tables</code>, and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">max_messages_per_poll</code>:
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>Worker invocation:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={workerSnippet}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock code={workerSnippet} lang="bash" />
      </div>

      <p>
        On Kubernetes, the operator runs the same worker from a <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">KafkaConnector</code> resource (the <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">krabka.io/cluster</code> label is required, and the database URL comes from a Secret key). The default worker image is <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">ghcr.io/krabka-io/krabka-connect-worker:v0.4.0</code>; set <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">spec.image</code> to use another tag or your own build:
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>KafkaConnector resource:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={connectorCrSnippet}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock code={connectorCrSnippet} lang="yaml" />
      </div>

      <h2 id="checkpoints" class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2 scroll-mt-24">Checkpoints and delivery</h2>
      <p>
        The worker writes with an idempotent producer and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">acks=all</code>, and stores the acknowledged Log Sequence Number (LSN) in the compacted <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">__krabka_connect_offsets</code> topic. It advances the PostgreSQL slot only after both the Kafka write and the checkpoint are durable. On restart, the worker resumes from the checkpoint. Delivery is at least once: a crash between the two writes can replay a batch of records.
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl p-5 border border-white/10 space-y-3 not-prose">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span>Running the Docker acceptance suite:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-colors text-xs" data-copy={acceptanceTestSnippet}>
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <CodeBlock code={acceptanceTestSnippet} lang="bash" />
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose pt-1">
        <a href={getPath('/features/connect')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Connect Feature Overview →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">High-level feature summary of Kafka Connect compatibility and MirrorMaker replication.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/krabka-io/gres" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">gres (broader krabka ecosystem) →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">A pure-Rust PostgreSQL-compatible SQL engine. Documented in its own repository.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
